---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro'
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro'
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro'
import { siteConfig } from '../data/siteConfig'
---

<Layout
  title="About point.dog Digital"
  description="point.dog is run by Mike Usry — operator-turned-agency. We build for businesses we'd run ourselves."
>
  <BreadcrumbSchema items={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'About', url: '/about' }]} />

  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="An operator running an agency."
    subtitle="point.dog is built on a simple bet: marketing built by people who actually run businesses works better than marketing built by people who never have."
    tone="primary"
  />

  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <Prose>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>point.dog Digital</strong> is run by Mike Usry from Athens, GA. We're a small,
        senior team. No junior account managers handing your work off to a developer who hands
        it off to a freelancer. The person you talk to ships your code.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we run our own businesses</h2>
      <p>
        Most agencies build sites and run ads for businesses they don't understand. We took
        the opposite path: we run <strong>five operating companies</strong> ourselves —
        across distribution, manufacturing, services, and construction. We feel the pain
        of every broken integration, every lossy pixel, every SaaS subscription that doesn't
        fit. Then we fix it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {
          siteConfig.operatingEntities.map((e) => (
            <li>
              <a href={e.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <strong>{e.name}</strong>
              </a>
              {' — '}
              {e.blurb}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2>What we believe about modern marketing</h2>
      <p>
        Google's PMax campaigns. Meta's Advantage+. Whatever AI-driven ad product launches
        this quarter. They all run on data. They all reward the advertisers feeding them
        clean first-party signal. They all punish the ones running stock pixels and lossy
        SaaS attribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most small businesses are losing this race because their stack wasn't built for it.
        Their POS doesn't talk to their CRM. Their site can't fire the conversion event
        the algorithm needs. Their attribution is "this person came from Google, probably."
      </p>
      <p>
        That's where we come in. We don't sell software. We sell the <em>marketing
        outcomes</em> that come from doing the technical work nobody else wants to do.
      </p>

      <h2>Honest about who we work with</h2>
      <p>
        We don't take every project. We're best for owner-operated businesses that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Are spending real money on ads and want them to actually work</li>
        <li>Have an existing stack that's mostly broken — POS, CRM, e-commerce, fundraising
        — that needs to be wired together properly</li>
        <li>Care about owning their data, not renting it</li>
        <li>Want a long-term partner, not a one-off project</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If that's you, <a href="/contact">let's talk</a>. We'll be honest about whether
        we're a fit.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </section>

  <CTASection />
</Layout>
